in order to accomplish this, i had to use the token from git hub as a security system to verify my git hub account, then i could git push the committed updates from the local repo to the remote repository.
in case token credentials expire, you can create a new token or renew the date of expiration, youll just have to enter the erasing command of previous credentials to update with new credentials.

